diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket's premise is incorrect — router4 is not down and has never been down during this investigation. Direct inspection of the device confirms the following healthy state: router4's LAN-facing interface eth0 is UP with IP 192.168.200.1/24, which is the correct default gateway for Location C (192.168.200.0/24). The FRR routing stack is fully operational — zebra, ripd, watchfrr, mgmtd, and staticd are all running. The RIP routing table is complete, containing connected routes for all three directly attached segments (192.168.200.0/24, 192.168.15.0/24, 172.25.1.0/24) plus RIP-learned routes to every other site in the topology, including a default route via 172.25.1.2. PC11 through PC14 all have correct IP addresses in the 192.168.200.11–14 range and each has their default gateway correctly set to 192.168.200.1. End-to-end connectivity tests confirm that PC11 and PC13 can both reach remote Location A hosts (172.16.10.4) with zero packet loss and normal latency (~2 ms). There is no fault, no misconfiguration, no dropped interface, and no routing blackhole anywhere in the Location C path. The reported outage does not exist in the live lab; this ticket is a false alarm and requires no corrective action.
=== END ===